  "ref": "DEU.2.21",
  "review_notes": [
    "`מִפְּנֵיהֶם` is one fused unit here: the ASV writes the single *before* for the preposition and its construct noun, so rule 30's one-rendering condition is met and neither morpheme is left `unrepresented`; headed on `פָּנֶה` as rule 23 heads `לִפְנֵי`, with the suffix taking its own *them* under rule 18.",
    "DEU.2.12 and DEU.2.22 write *from before*, a word for each morpheme, and are split there under rule 2. The chapter's other one-word compounds — *aforetime* in 2.10, 2.12 and 2.20, *before* in 2.31, 2.33 and 2.36, *upon* and *because of* in 2.25 — fuse on the same terms as this one."
